(5869016, 851761, 114625, '<td valign="top">This is beautiful!  I have an Eskie also and he is the same - LOVES the snow!  Thank you for your beautiful photo of a beautiful dog (and breed)!  It truly looks like bliss to her.</td>', 'This is beautiful!  I have an Eskie also and he is the same - LOVES the snow!  Thank you for your beautiful photo of a beautiful dog (and breed)!  It truly looks like bliss to her.', '2010-02-16 12:13:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5869373, 851205, 62357, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>I do not know I can add too much of value to this critique.  I think your image is interesting and blown out highlights in the sky add a certain something to it.  However, I do believe that your score suffered due to the large number of people who did not feel it truly depicted cold.  As noted by the comments of others, many felt it rather portrayed wet.  I would contend that typically being wet is kind of cold, but many are very literal in the interpretation of the challenge topic.<br/> <br/>I feel your composition is perhaps a little tight, I would prefer to see a bit more space to the left of the guy (as I am looking at the image).  To me the image looks like it''s been cropped in PS rather than framed in the camera (not saying there is anything wrong with that, I just feel in this case it is a bit too tight).<br/> <br/>I liked the concept of this image a lot, and am sorry it didn''t score higher.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  I do not know I can add too much of value to this critique.  I think your image is interesting and blown out highlights in the sky add a certain something to it.  However, I do believe that your score suffered due to the large number of people who did not feel it truly depicted cold.  As noted by the comments of others, many felt it rather portrayed wet.  I would contend that typically being wet is kind of cold, but many are very literal in the interpretation of the challenge topic. I feel your composition is perhaps a little tight, I would prefer to see a bit more space to the left of the guy (as I am looking at the image).  To me the image looks like it''s been cropped in PS rather than framed in the camera (not saying there is anything wrong with that, I just feel in this case it is a bit too tight). I liked the concept of this image a lot, and am sorry it didn''t score higher.', '2010-02-16 14:41:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5869835, 850962, 76335, '<td valign="top">I admire you for entering this. Clearly it took a beating, but those who loved it really loved it. I didn''t vote in the challenge, and this is my first time seeing it. All that white negative space does have a chilling effect. And if I hold my head just so, I think I even see a horizon... <br/> <br/>''Cool'' shot.</td>', 'I admire you for entering this. Clearly it took a beating, but those who loved it really loved it. I didn''t vote in the challenge, and this is my first time seeing it. All that white negative space does have a chilling effect. And if I hold my head just so, I think I even see a horizon...  ''Cool'' shot.', '2010-02-16 21:21:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5870677, 851243, 109353, '<td valign="top">Hey stop it now !<br/>It takes me so much time to make my place in the 55mm f/3.5 page and you still want to be alone ! :D<br/>Ok I have to admit this is a really nice shot. I can''t believe it''s still sharp with three extension tubes. Good to know ;)</td>', 'Hey stop it now !It takes me so much time to make my place in the 55mm f/3.5 page and you still want to be alone ! :DOk I have to admit this is a really nice shot. I can''t believe it''s still sharp with three extension tubes. Good to know ;)', '2010-02-17 05:49:17.000000', NULL, 0),
